B.ml=new A.eS("The Beauty of the Attire: ",null,B.aN,B.cS)
B.mm=new A.eS("Nepal is a beautiful country filled with diverse cultures and traditions. Among them, the Tajpuriya community has its own unique cultural dress that reflects its rich heritage and identity. Just like every caste or community has its own traditional attire based on culture, the Tajpuriya people also proudly wear their traditional dress with pride.\n\n",null,B.aN,null)
B.mn=new A.eS("Tajpuriya women wear a dress called Petani, which comes in various colors such as black, red, green, and brown. It is typically paired with a blouse and traditional jewelry like Matha, Churi, Sipitar, Sati ban, Sana, Jhumka (made of silver or gold), Satasarir har, Donoriya Bichha and Taka Har. They also wear Chandra Har, Kammar Badh and Bichhiya.\n\n",null,B.aN,null)
B.mo=new A.eS("Tajpuriya boys and girls look incredibly beautiful in their cultural dress. There\u2019s truly no need for many words \u2014 their appearance speaks for itself. Whether it's the charm of tradition or the elegance of the dress, the Tajpuriya look is something special and worth admiring. \ud83d\ude0a\u2728",null,B.aN,null)
B.mp=new A.eS(", unlike other communities. A special item in their attire is the Gamchha, a traditional cloth available in many colors like red, yellow, white, and more.\n\n",null,B.aN,null)
B.mq=new A.eS("For Men: ",null,B.aN,B.cS)
B.mr=new A.eS("An interesting note is that Tajpuriya women do not wear nose pins",null,B.aN,B.cS)
B.ms=new A.eS("Tajpuriya men wear a Dhoti in white or other light colors. They also wear a Gamchha and a white vest, creating a simple yet dignified traditional look.\n\n",null,B.aN,null)
B.mt=new A.eS("For Women: ",null,B.aN,B.cS)
